{"assets":["/statement-assets/c893d8148155e9f96bef40dc5029320151da9c48357d03a963f021e9bb3b30de.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"690","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C3. Brain Network (hard)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Breaking news from zombie neurology! It turns out that – contrary to previous beliefs – every zombie is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"born"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with a single brain, and only later it evolves into a complicated brain structure. In fact, whenever a zombie consumes a brain, a new brain appears in its nervous system and gets immediately connected to one of the already existing brains using a single brain connector. Researchers are now interested in monitoring the brain latency of a zombie. Your task is to write a program which, given a history of evolution of a zombie's nervous system, computes its brain latency at every stage."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" – the number of brains in the final nervous system ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 200000"},{"kind":"text","text":"). In the second line a history of zombie's nervous system evolution is given. For convenience, we number all the brains by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1, 2, ..., n"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the same order as they appear in the nervous system (the zombie is born with a single brain, number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and subsequently brains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2, 3, ..., n"},{"kind":"text","text":" are added). The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p2, p3, ..., pn"},{"kind":"text","text":", meaning that after a new brain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" is added to the system, it gets connected to a parent-brain "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c893d8148155e9f96bef40dc5029320151da9c48357d03a963f021e9bb3b30de.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated numbers – the brain latencies after the brain number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" is added, for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k = 2, 3, ..., n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n1\n2\n2\n1\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2 2 3 4 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C3","problemCode":"690C3","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/690/problem/C3"}